{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Module","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.signPattern_forces_deuteron_floor_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.signPattern_forces_deuteron_floor_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaIsospinChannel.lean#L153-L163","doc":"The same floor stated against a ceiling on the bare deviation: if `μ_G − 1 ≤ ε`,\nthe C1 sign pattern forces `B_{T=0} > α·log(1/ε)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.signPattern_forces_deuteron_floor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.signPattern_forces_deuteron_floor","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaIsospinChannel.lean#L139-L151","doc":"**The deuteron floor forced by the C1 sign pattern.** Under the live law\n`B = −α·log μ` with `α > 0`: if `μ₊ + μ₋ = μ_G`, the `T = 1` channel is unbound\n(`μ₊ > 1`) and the `T = 0` ratio is positive, then the `T = 0` binding exceeds\n`α·log(1/(μ_G − 1))`. With `μ_G − 1 = h⁴·c(q)` of order `10⁻³` at the anchor, this is a\ndeuteron bound by several `α`, which is what the pattern costs under C1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.some_channel_unbound_of_bare_unbound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.some_channel_unbound_of_bare_unbound","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaIsospinChannel.lean#L121-L133","doc":"**At least one relative channel is unbound.** A convex combination with positive\nweights that exceeds `1` has a term exceeding `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.plus_le_one_of_minus_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.plus_le_one_of_minus_ge","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaIsospinChannel.lean#L115-L119","doc":"Contrapositive: if the `T = 0` ratio is at least `μ_G − 1`, the `T = 1` channel is\nbound or marginal (`μ₊ ≤ 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.minus_lt_of_signPattern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.minus_lt_of_signPattern","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaIsospinChannel.lean#L109-L113","doc":"In a sum rule `μ₊ + μ₋ = μ_G`, the `T = 1` channel is unbound and the `T = 0` channel\nhas positive ratio only if `μ₋ < μ_G − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.relative_channel_average","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.relative_channel_average","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaIsospinChannel.lean#L95-L101","doc":"**The C4/C5 average.** With channel weights `w_T = tr(W·P_T)/tr(W)` and relative ratios\n`μ_Tʳᵉˡ = tr(W·G·P_T)/tr(W·P_T)`, the bare ratio is their weighted sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.channel_ratio_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.channel_ratio_sum","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaIsospinChannel.lean#L89-L93","doc":"**The C1 sum rule.** Dividing `trace_splits` by the free trace: the `T = 1` and `T = 0`\nratios of composition C1 sum to the bare γγ ratio `μ_G = tr(W·G)/tr(W)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.trace_splits","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.trace_splits","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaIsospinChannel.lean#L77-L81","doc":"**C1 at the trace level.** For any `R`-linear trace, the two projected bonded traces\nadd up to the bare bonded trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.bonded_word_splits","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.bonded_word_splits","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaIsospinChannel.lean#L71-L75","doc":"**C1 at the operator level.** Right-multiplying the bonded word by the two projectors\nand adding gives back the bonded word: `X·P₊ + X·P₋ = X` for every `X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.proj_add_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaIsospinChannel.proj_add_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaIsospinChannel.lean#L62-L69","doc":"The projectors are complementary — restated here (the same identity as\n`QOU.QBeta.InterfaceScalar.proj_add_eq_one`) so this file depends on Mathlib only. ","signatureChunk":0}]}